# Section theme photos

When creating or renaming a pursuit section card (`.sec-card`), always assign a banner photo that matches the section’s meaning.

## Rules

- Use `window.__secImgFor(sectionName)` / the `IMG` + `KEYWORDS` maps in `dashboard.html` — do not reuse a generic lifestyle/vibes image when a better thematic match exists.
- Today **LIFESTYLE** section banner is `manus-storage/pursuit-lifestyle_577937e8.jpg` (Celine sunglasses + coffee + YSL bag flat-lay — the original curated lifestyle card). NOT boutique / woman looking at a shirt, NOT a coffee cup with no glasses. Do not restyle previous days’ lifestyle cards.
- Travel-related sections (`travel`, `travel-ready`, `traveler`, trip, flight, luggage, airport, packing) must use `manus-storage/pursuit-travel.jpg`.
- Returns / refund / exchange sections must use `manus-storage/pursuit-returns-v2.jpg` (cash / money back — not the shopped lifestyle flat-lay, not packages, not a cute piggy bank).
- Pickups sections must use `manus-storage/pursuit-pickups.jpg` (store / curbside pickup bag — not money, not returns cash).
- Quantum **section** must use `manus-storage/zone-quantum-v15.jpg?v=observe` — deep cinematic still: an observing eye in dark glass, a golden vibrating filament of entangled strings/membranes, interference fringes in the void. NOT the old two-dot v14 graphic, NOT lab laser benches, NOT a coin, NOT Pink Floyd prism, NOT calcite, NOT plasma globe / IBM fridge / CERN / soap film / TV-static.
- Power **section** banner is `manus-storage/mock-power.jpg` (chess king). **Leverage is a card inside Power**, photo `manus-storage/pursuit-leverage-v4.jpg?v=key` (small key in a massive lock = small instrument, outsized access). NOT chess, NOT wrench wall, seesaw, crowbar, courthouse, fulcrum.
- On travel sections, put past-tense status verbs (e.g. packed, picked up) at the **end of the task status/progress bar**, not grayed inside the task title.
- If no suitable local image exists for a new theme, add one under `manus-storage/` (self-hosted; no CDN dependency) and register it in both the exact-name `IMG` map and the `KEYWORDS` list.
- After adding/renaming a section, run or rely on `__normalizeSecCards` so the photo + theme class stay in sync.
- When a **new** pursuit card is introduced on a day, also add an **empty** copy of that card to **every following day** (including flow-only days — seed a full `.sec-grid` if missing), **unless the user explicitly scopes it to one day** (e.g. pickups on Jul 25 only). Empty cards stay compact (square header + bottom-right `+` only) until tasks are added. Recent forward-fill names: `momentum`, `UX Design`, `workflow`, `Power`, `Frequency`, `postal`, `traveler`, `returns`.
- Pursuit cards stay **square**. Empty = 148px full-bleed photo + `+`. With tasks ≈ 210px.
- With-tasks composition = **full-bleed photo vision board**: the whole card is the image; each task is a small **beige ripped-paper scrap** with Reenie Beanie handwriting. Card stays **square** and **grows with item count** (`--vb-size`); scraps sit in a soft grid so they don’t overlap. Title stays on the photo. Users can drag the bottom-right resize handle (`.card-sized`); never wipe that size in sync unless it’s non-square / too small for the scraps.
- Items inside each pursuit card are **numbered** (1, 2, 3…) per card.
- Jul 25/26 Flow: keep a dedicated `.gsep-retreat-card` **after** the flow timeline card. Never delete it in flow-chart-card dedupe (pursuits panel also uses `.flow-chart-card`).
- Flow timeline reorder is **global for every day**: keep Sortable attached to every `.flow-timeline-list`; never destroy/rebuild lists just to sync pins (append-only); respect `__flowReorderCooldown` after drag so sync doesn’t wipe order.
- Keep assets local under `manus-storage/` — do not point card banners at Manus or other remote CDNs.
